menu "Floppy example"

    config EXAMPLE_FORCE_FULL_SPEED
        bool "Run the high-speed USB port at full speed only"
        depends on SOC_USB_UTMI_PHY_NUM > 0
        default y
        help
            USB floppy drives are full-speed devices. Behind a high-speed hub they need the hub's Transaction
            Translator, which the ESP USB Host Library doesn't support: the drive is not enumerated ("transaction
            translator (TT) is not supported"). Running the port at full speed makes the hub work at full speed too,
            so the drive behind it is reachable. Not needed when the drive is plugged in directly.

    config EXAMPLE_WRITE_TEST
        bool "Write a test file to the disk"
        default n
        help
            Writes ESPTEST.TXT to the root directory, reads it back and compares.

    config EXAMPLE_FORMAT
        bool "Format the disk (erases it!)"
        default n
        help
            Low-level formats the disk to its largest format, with verify, then creates an empty FAT12 file system
            labelled ESP-FLOPPY. Everything on the disk is lost.

endmenu
